# Reports how long the transfer took, which is a property of the moment. Verified by hand;
# the shape is stable, the numbers are not.
Print several facts about a transfer at once

# The -v transcript carries the negotiated TLS parameters, the resolved IP and per-connection
# detail, none of which is reproducible. Verified by hand against https://example.com. This is
# the only example left that needs a real HTTPS host: the -k pair moved to the local server's
# --tls mode, where a self-signed certificate makes the flag actually change the outcome.
Watch the full TLS handshake and request

# Returns the caller's own public IP, which differs for every reader by definition. Verified
# by hand from a networked Debian trixie box.
See the public IP a request would come from
